<article class="env-lemma" id="02OP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02OP">Lemma <span data-tag="02OP">31.15.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $D_1$, $D_2$ be effective Cartier divisors on $S$. Let $D = D_1 + D_2$. Then there is a unique isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O}_ S(D_1) \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ S} \mathcal{O}_ S(D_2) \longrightarrow \mathcal{O}_ S(D)  \]
</div>
  <p> which maps $1_{D_1} \otimes 1_{D_2}$ to $1_ D$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>